  "body": "Part of #2007.\n\nMaintainer in chat, 2026-11-15: \"That tool editor issue is a P3\".\n\n## What happens\n\nThe tool editor has two previews:\n- `draw_tool_preview` (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/pages.rs:847-851`): the side profile and the body envelope.\n- `tool_body_page::preview_3d` in the Body tab of `tool_profile_page::third_column` (L852-856).\n\n#2005 (PR #2010) stops the side preview from drawing the body and the spun profile over each other. #2009 shows the conservative floor of a machine-default holder.\n\n## What to do\n\n- Keep one side preview in the Properties tool page. It shows the tool, the holder and the checked envelope (the shape from `tool_body::judged`).\n- Remove the second (3D) preview from the editor.\n- Keep each file below about 400 lines.\n\n## Done means:\n\n- The tool page shows one preview.\n- The structural test pins one preview and no 3D preview.\n- The preview draws the same holder shape that the collision check reads. A UI test pins this for an explicit body and for no body.\n- No snapshot PNG changes. The PR has before and after screenshots.\n\nOrder: after #2005 and the layout sub-issue.\n",
